From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PATCH] ART: explicitly zero discarded memory in x86 host tools

Actual QEMU 6.2 linux-user returns success for MADV_DONTNEED while all
65536 patterned anonymous bytes remain nonzero; the same native ARM64
probe clears them. Select ART's existing kMadviseZeroes=false paths for
x86 hosts so reused heap objects are zeroed. Keep Baker/read-barrier
checks, GC and the Android target-runtime branch unchanged.

--- a/runtime/mem_map.h
+++ b/runtime/mem_map.h
@@ -41,7 +41,10 @@
 #define USE_ART_LOW_4G_ALLOCATOR 0
 #endif
 
-#ifdef __linux__
+// QEMU 6.2 linux-user acknowledges MADV_DONTNEED without discarding or
+// zeroing anonymous pages. Host x86 ART must use its existing explicit
+// zeroing paths; Android target runtimes keep native Linux semantics.
+#if defined(__linux__) && (defined(__ANDROID__) || (!defined(__x86_64__) && !defined(__i386__)))
 static constexpr bool kMadviseZeroes = true;
 #else
 static constexpr bool kMadviseZeroes = false;
